    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a052943_943c5c88",
        "filename": "src/core/SkPaintParamsKey.h",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-15T14:53:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we need to make SkPaintParamsKey wrapped in a unique_ptr here. SkTArray\u003cuint8_t\u003e already gives us one step of indirection and supports variable size. We can return an invalid key that has 0 size in its data array if the builder is invalid.\n\nThe biggest reason I\u0027m pushing for this is that in the tight loop of DrawPass::Make we\u0027re going to hopefully reuse the same builder and construct a key, query, and continue. Ideally we can then add a snapView() or similar to the builder that wraps its data buffer as a key w/o doing any copying or malloc. Copying would only happen in findOrCreate() if we needed to insert an entry. Otherwise once we have the uniqueID we can reset the builder and no longer need the key view.\n\nWhile we\u0027re not ready for that yet, adding unique_ptr and then pulling it back just seems like extra work when we can have snap() report failures in other ways.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "43822601ae4532e34b821d3e58cc1f626f223893",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
